# The harness CLIs the REQUIRED checks install, pinned once (`.tool-versions`
# format: one package and exactly one x.y.z version per line). The npm ones are
# keyed by package name; `goose` is Goose's vendor installer, which takes its
# version as GOOSE_VERSION.
#
# Scope: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` only — the jobs a merge waits on. An
# unpinned install there fails a passing tree whenever a publisher is
# mid-release (Copilot 1.0.115 shipped its package before its darwin-arm64
# platform package and failed `check (macos-latest)`). The paid `e2e-*` and
# dispatch-only `explore-*` workflows gate nothing and deliberately track the
# latest releases: that is what still catches an upstream CLI change. Cursor's
# installer (cursor.com/install) bakes its version into the script it serves
# and takes no version input, so ci.yml's Cursor install cannot be pinned.
#
# scripts/check-harness-cli-pins.sh holds ci.yml to this file: every npm
# global install there names its package's pin, and every Goose install passes
# it. To move a pin: change it here, run the check, fix each ci.yml line it
# names, and let the PR's `check (macos-latest)` prove the new version installs.
